**8. Use the notes study data to graphically explore the relationship of method of note taking to later recall. Your graph should illustrate whether the type of lecture moderates the effect of note taking method on recall.**

```{r}

# Using read_excel since file was Excel.

notes_study <- read_excel(here("data", "Notes Data.xlsx"))

```


```{r}

# Converting lecture and notes to factors.

notes_study$lecture <- factor(notes_study$lecture, labels = c("Lecture 1", "Lecture 2"))
notes_study$notes <- factor(notes_study$notes, labels = c("Laptop", "Handwritten", "No Notes"))

# Create interaction plot.

ggplot(notes_study, aes(x = notes, y = score, fill = notes)) +
  geom_boxplot(alpha = 0.7) +
  stat_summary(fun = mean, geom = "point", shape = 20, size = 3, color = "black", position = position_dodge(width = 0.75)) +
  facet_wrap(~ lecture) +
  labs(
    title = "Effect of Note-Taking Method on Recall by Lecture Type",
    x = "Note-Taking Method",
    y = "Recall Score",
    fill = "Notes"
  ) +
  theme_minimal()


```


